WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.180
Question four.

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:07.505
Step one: macro scan. It asks what kind of device the rain-gauge sensor is.

00:00:07.505 --> 00:00:10.709
One mark. Command words: “belongs to”.

00:00:10.709 --> 00:00:12.227
Step two: denoise.

00:00:12.227 --> 00:00:17.033
Useful, in yellow: rain-gauge sensor, real-time rainfall.

00:00:17.033 --> 00:00:18.635
In cyan: “measure”.

00:00:18.635 --> 00:00:24.032
Useless red herring: where the weather station is — kick it out.

00:00:24.032 --> 00:00:25.549
Step three: draft.

00:00:25.549 --> 00:00:29.850
Outside values enter the system through the sensor.

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:32.632
Flow goes from outside to inside.

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.572
Flowing in means input.

00:00:34.572 --> 00:00:36.005
Step four: P O E.

00:00:36.005 --> 00:00:39.378
B, output device: wrong direction — cut.

00:00:39.378 --> 00:00:43.257
C, display device: no display mentioned — cut.

00:00:43.257 --> 00:00:47.304
D, printing device: no printing mentioned — cut.

00:00:47.304 --> 00:00:54.387
Step five: sanity check and lock. Data flows into the system, consistent with input.

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:56.664
So the correct answer is A.
